        "original_id": "c0e0905a-7963-55e3-a9f3-e39c3ffbd974",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rosario Castellanos Figueroa, Arthur Hailey\n- Places: Centro Cultural Bella Época, Rosario Castellanos bookshop\n- Roles: poet, author, novelist\n- Topics: Mexican literature, British-Canadian fiction, bookstores in Latin America\n\nFacts:\n- Rosario Castellanos Figueroa was born on 25 May 1925 and died on 7 August 1974.\n- Arthur Hailey was born on 5 April 1920 and died on 24 November 2004.\n- Rosario Castellanos Figueroa was a Mexican poet and author.\n- Arthur Hailey was a British-Canadian novelist whose plot-driven storylines were set against the backdrops of various industries.\n- Centro Cultural Bella Época includes the Rosario Castellanos bookshop.\n- The Rosario Castellanos bookshop is claimed to be the largest bookshop in Latin America.\n- The Rosario Castellanos bookshop carries over 35 thousand different titles and includes a children’s area, a coffee shop, and reading facilities.",
